      It means this printf will print any arbitrary value. But notice that even for any arbitrary value, the no. of bytes output by inner printf would be non-zero. 
      And those no. of bytes will work as argument to outer printf. 
      The outer printf will print that many no. of bytes and return non-zero value always. So the condition for if is also true always. 
